xnu 0455: keep the reboot reason and the last line before the reset

Measured 2026-11-26: after a boot whose ring stopped at a failed reboot, a
"hardreset" from the host reset the SoC but landed on boot_b, not in
fastboot. Two causes, both in the escape path:

- hardreset reused mondrian_set_reset_reason, whose one-shot flag an earlier
  attempt had already set, so the PMIC restart reason -- the only interface
  this bootloader reads, a BCB alone boots the active slot -- was never
  written. Force it.
- The "PSCI system reset to fastboot" line is printed before the SMC and was
  never flushed, so a reset the monitor refuses reads as a boot that stopped
  at the previous step. Flush before the call.

The control channel also answers "bcb <command>" now, so a host can point
the boot control block at the bootloader without resetting anything; the
usb-ring tool has been sending that command to a kernel that ignored it.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 7717f78..c5a26a5 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -1516,7 +1516,7 @@ mondrian_log_flush_now(void)
  * Only the command field of the BCB is touched; the A/B metadata lives in the
  * rest of the block.
  */
-static int
+int
 mondrian_ufs_bcb_set(const char *command)
 {
 	uint8_t *b = (uint8_t *)(su.dma + DMA_BOUNCE);
@@ -1668,6 +1668,12 @@ mondrian_reset_to_bootloader(int recovery)
 	mondrian_set_reset_reason(recovery);
 	printf("MONDRIAN RESET: PSCI system reset to %s\n",
 	    recovery ? "recovery" : "fastboot");
+	/*
+	 * Flush here: this is the last line before the monitor. Everything the
+	 * reset path prints after it stays in memory, and a reset the monitor
+	 * refuses then reads as a boot that stopped at the previous step.
+	 */
+	mondrian_log_flush_now();
 	(void)mondrian_smc(0x84000009ull);      /* PSCI_SYSTEM_RESET */
 	/*
 	 * PSCI returned, so no reset happened. Dropping PS_HOLD collapses the
@@ -1778,7 +1784,14 @@ mondrian_reboot_to_fastboot(void)
 void
 mondrian_hard_reset(void)
 {
-	printf("MONDRIAN HARD RESET: skipping the sync and the bcb\n");
+	/*
+	 * The restart reason is what the bootloader actually reads: a BCB alone
+	 * boots the active slot (measured 2026-11-26, a hard reset after a failed
+	 * reboot landed on boot_b). Force the write -- a reboot thread that hung
+	 * after setting the flag would otherwise leave a stale reason behind.
+	 */
+	mondrian_reset_reason_set = 0;
+	printf("MONDRIAN HARD RESET: reason and PSCI only\n");
 	mondrian_log_flush_now();
 	mondrian_reset_to_bootloader(0);
 	printf("MONDRIAN HARD RESET: returned\n");
